---
// Draft scoped notice: Cyrus must approve the exact wording before activation.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Website analytics privacy"
  description="Your optional website analytics choice, the data involved, and how to withdraw."
  canonicalUrl="https://jamula.net/privacy/"
>
  <article class="privacy">
    <h1>Website analytics privacy</h1>
    <p>
      Updated November 2, 2026. This notice covers optional analytics on Jamula's public website.
    </p>
    <h2>Your choice comes first</h2>
    <p>
      Jamula, Inc. uses Google Analytics only if you choose Accept analytics. Before acceptance, or
      after rejection, this integration does not load Google's tag or send analytics requests. The
      website works without analytics. Global Privacy Control keeps analytics off.
    </p>
    <h2>What is measured</h2>
    <p>
      We request page views and counts of contact-link clicks. A contact click is an expression of
      interest, not proof that an inquiry was sent or received. We do not send the destination email
      address, link text, URL query strings, fragments, form contents, or your email message.
      Unknown page paths are grouped as a not-found page.
    </p>
    <p>
      After acceptance, Google receives browser and device information, cookie identifiers and
      network information needed to process requests, including your IP address. This is not
      anonymous processing. Google Analytics may derive session, first-visit and engagement
      information as part of its operation. We do not request advertising personalization, Google
      Signals, user-provided data, or cross-domain linking. Jamula.com and Jamula.net use separate
      measurement IDs; your preference is not shared between domains or between apex and www.
    </p>
    <h2>Storage and retention</h2>
    <p>
      This browser stores your choice, hostname, purpose, notice version and time in local storage,
      without a personal identifier. The choice is valid for up to 180 days; the stored record can
      remain until you replace it or clear site data. A changed purpose or notice version requires
      a new choice. If storage is unavailable, analytics stays off. After acceptance, this
      integration uses host-only session cookies with names beginning with jamula_ga.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our required Google Analytics user/event retention setting is the shortest available option
      (two months), with reset on new activity off. This is an account-side setting that a property
      administrator must verify; website code cannot set it. That setting does not limit Google's
      standard aggregated reports.
    </p>
    <h2>Withdrawal and requests</h2>
    <p>
      Use Withdraw analytics in the footer at any time. Withdrawal stops future collection by this
      integration, clears its cookies on this hostname and reloads the page to unload Google's code.
      It cannot recall requests already sent or automatically erase data already held by Google.
      Clear site data to remove the locally saved preference; you will be asked again, with
      analytics off by default. Each hostname has a separate choice.
    </p>
    <p>
      For privacy questions or requests concerning previously collected data, use the contact
      details on the <a href="/">home page</a>. Do not send sensitive information. Requests to
      Google may require an administrator and may be limited by what can be linked to your browser.
      Google processes data on its infrastructure, which may involve international transfers. See{" "}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a> and
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">
        how Google uses information from partner sites
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    max-width: var(--j-content-width);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: var(--j-space-8) var(--j-space-6);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--j-text-3xl);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--j-text-xl);
    margin-block-start: var(--j-space-8);
  }

  p {
    margin-block-start: var(--j-space-4);
  }
</style>
